===========================================================
Generative AI Use
===========================================================
Generative AI used: Claude (Anthropic, claude.ai)

Prompts used (paraphrased):
  - Make the message queue use the worker's PID as mtype for direct delivery
    and the OSS PID for replies.
  - Add signal handling that cleans up shared memory and message queues on
    SIGINT, SIGTERM, and SIGALRM, and prints a final report before exiting.
  - Fix the ready queue so it prints before dequeuing, not after.
  - Fix the process table to print to both stdout and the log file.
  - Fix the CPU utilization formula to match the spec wording (overhead/idle
    time, not worker run time).
  - Fix the log line counter to count actual newlines rather than call count.
  - Add a clear log message when the 3-second wall-clock limit is hit.
  - Review all files against the rubric for anything missing.

Summary: Claude was used to help complete this project.
The scheduler logic, IPC design, signal handling, and cleanup
all worked. Several smaller issues were caught and fixed through iterative
review: the queue print order, the process table not printing to stdout, the
CPU utilization formula being backwards relative to the spec, and the log
line counter being per-call instead of per-newline. Overall Claude was very
useful for both generating and reviewing the code.
